From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: McKernel Rust Port <mckernel-rust@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 17:18:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] x86/pvh: annotate the direct PVH entry as no-ENDBR

The exact Rocky 10.2 kernel reaches the final vmlinux.o objtool pass with
IBT enabled and reports a relocation from pvh_start_xen address arithmetic
to the same direct Xen PVH ABI entry.  The relocation is never used as an
indirect branch target.

Classify that relocation with ANNOTATE_NOENDBR, whose contract is precisely
to suppress relocation-to-!ENDBR diagnostics when the relocation cannot be
used for an indirect call.  startup_xen uses the same annotation pattern.
This adds only objtool discard metadata and changes no executed PVH bytes.

This is a local Rocky compatibility annotation, not a backport of upstream
commit 5c6808d1a9dd83853ff39684aeb812be39e108e8, which later removes the
absolute relocation as part of a broader PVH cleanup.

